#15003
On The King's Road Outside A Castle~
   The road ends before King Welmar's castle. It was built for beauty, not
for war: white stone, slim towers, carved windows. Lately someone has tried
to make up for that. The windows have been narrowed to arrow slits with raw
new masonry, and the moat has been dug deeper. A drawbridge crosses the moat
to the north; the road leads back west.
~
